\tag{fdip}
\title{Several species under one charged rotation}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{When several species of Grassmann generators share one rotation parameter,
each can carry a different integer power of that parameter. Which choices
preserve the coefficient functional on the combined algebra?}

\p{The generator spaces are finite-dimensional over a field with #{2\ne 0}.
For complex Ginsparg–Wilson operators, the kernel indices give the exponent
of the rotation.}
